## Decision matrix

“Accept” here applies only to the stated design boundary or invariant. “Conditional” leaves an unimplemented candidate eligible for a later exact contract. Neither word grants implementation, schema, API or runtime acceptance.

| Proposed choice | Decision | Exact source-bound condition or limit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Eight lifecycle actions | **Accept the limited design scope.** | Exactly `start`, `hold`, `resume`, `complete`, `cancel`, `archive`, `restore`, `reopen` matches the pinned `ProjectAction` union and strict command schema. Create, membership, owner transfer and every other operation remain outside edition 1. This grants no native command authority. [Proposal lines 7-9](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-authority-transaction-evidence/docs/agency-projects/privacy-lifecycle-representation-proposal.md:7), [pinned command schema](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/6855645499b5f5878f7b2d2eb431dd6e6d4b7fbc/src/features/agency-projects/projectSchemas.ts#L14-L18) |
| Validated normalization | **Conditionally accept as a specification candidate.** | Use the actual emitted canonical UUIDs, accepted safe integer revision and validated reason. `canonicalUuidSchema` lowercases valid UUID input; it does not require lowercase input. `reasonSchema` trims, bounds at 2,000 code units, rejects disallowed controls and format-only nonempty text, and preserves accepted content. Its format-character removal is only a validity predicate, not an output transformation. Omitted or accepted empty reason can map to null. Invalid text must remain invalid, rather than being stripped into null. No Unicode normalization, reason case conversion or locale formatting is approved. [Pinned value schemas](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/6855645499b5f5878f7b2d2eb431dd6e6d4b7fbc/src/features/agency-projects/valueSchemas.ts#L3-L20) |
| Fixed-order request bytes and discriminator | **Conditional design input; production comparison contract unselected.** | The proposed tuple below unambiguously covers actor, intent, project, action, expected revision and normalized reason when it is built exclusively from validated primitive values. Preserve its exact field order and the stated well-formed `JSON.stringify` escaping before UTF-8 encoding. Transport/CSRF data, session contents, clocks and generated event/result IDs do not belong in this semantic value. This is an Agency candidate discriminator, not a new `PrivacyContext` purpose. No codec implementation or cross-runtime qualification exists in this proposal. [Proposal lines 13-19](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-authority-transaction-evidence/docs/agency-projects/privacy-lifecycle-representation-proposal.md:13) |
| Request namespace versus receipt uniqueness | **Unresolved integration contract.** | The older notation keys receipts by actor/operation/intent; the candidate tuple includes action. The exact mapping of the eight actions to persisted `operation` and logical-intent identity must be pinned before claiming that changing an action necessarily reaches the same receipt and produces a conflict. Different encoded bytes alone do not establish which record will be looked up. This review selects neither an operation vocabulary nor a new uniqueness rule. [Prior notation lines 134-166](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-core-schema-review/docs/agency-projects/schema-review/projectCore.schema.ts.txt:134) |
| Private comparison record | **Accept the privacy requirement; interface and format remain unselected.** | Keep normalized comparison input, keyed bytes, domain/encoding edition, format metadata and opaque comparison-key reference private. They must not appear in routine DTOs, logs, telemetry or an existence probe. No raw hash, publicly exposed fingerprint, alternate token wrapper or invented key identifier is approved. Comparison-key and encryption-key references must remain separately specified; no shared-key relationship or derivation is selected. [Proposal lines 17-19](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-authority-transaction-evidence/docs/agency-projects/privacy-lifecycle-representation-proposal.md:17) |
| Four-store protected history slot | **Conditional design option; physical placement unselected.** | It may remain a candidate for these eight actions. The eventual contract must enforce immutable event facts independently from authorized content/disposition mutation, required payload insertion, safe projections and participating writer fences. Separate column names alone enforce none of that. A whole-row immutable policy would prevent later disposition; a general history-row update grant could alter facts. No specific enforcement mechanism or SQL is selected here. The proposal itself acknowledges this separation. [Proposal lines 23-25](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-authority-transaction-evidence/docs/agency-projects/privacy-lifecycle-representation-proposal.md:23) |
| Separate fifth content store | **Unselected alternative; not mandated by the current evidence.** | Explicit content states can be specified for either placement. If a separate lifecycle/access boundary is required, the fifth store needs its own owner decision, source/copy classification and accepted same-project linkage. Its earlier composite FK and at-most-one-payload PK are notation only and do not enforce required insertion or disposition. Neither a missing row nor deleting that row is an approved disposition record. [Prior notation lines 168-196](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-core-schema-review/docs/agency-projects/schema-review/projectCore.schema.ts.txt:168) |
| Immutable facts versus reason copies | **Accept the separation invariant.** | Preserve event/project/action/policy/revision/state/recorder/correlation facts independently from sensitive content. Do not persist or project the existing pure `ProjectTransitionReceipt` unchanged: it contains plaintext `reason`. That private in-memory policy result is not an approved request receipt, routine activity record or HTTP DTO. The future writer/projection boundary must consume that value without creating another reason copy. [Pinned receipt type](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/6855645499b5f5878f7b2d2eb431dd6e6d4b7fbc/src/features/agency-projects/projectLifecycle.ts#L25-L33), [pinned result construction](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/6855645499b5f5878f7b2d2eb431dd6e6d4b7fbc/src/features/agency-projects/projectLifecycle.ts#L90-L98) |
| `not-supplied`, `present`, `disposed` | **Accept these semantic distinctions; disposition implementation remains unselected.** | `not-supplied` denotes no accepted initial reason and no protected/key metadata. A supplied nonempty reason requires `present` with protected bytes, envelope format and opaque encryption-key reference. `disposed` must remain distinguishable from original absence and retain only separately approved minimal provenance after protected bytes are removed. Previously supplied content cannot be relabeled as never supplied. Missing/unresolvable key is unavailable material, not disposition or erasure evidence. Actual permitted kinds, retained fields, actor authority, timestamps, writers and intervals still need decisions. [Proposal line 25](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-authority-transaction-evidence/docs/agency-projects/privacy-lifecycle-representation-proposal.md:25) |
| Reason-required initial event/payload | **Accept the atomicity invariant.** | `hold`, `cancel`, `archive`, `restore`, `reopen` require a nonempty validated reason. A successful initial commit must contain the event and `present` payload together; initial `disposed` cannot satisfy that requirement. For optional-reason actions, a supplied accepted nonempty reason still needs protection. No transaction rollback, database constraint or native writer qualification is established by this review. [Pinned transition policy](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/6855645499b5f5878f7b2d2eb431dd6e6d4b7fbc/src/features/agency-projects/projectLifecycle.ts#L64-L83) |
| Project/event reason AAD candidate | **Conditional binding specification; actual authenticated envelope contract unselected.** | The second tuple below identifies the Agency reason domain, authoritative project, exact history event and content kind/schema. Its two edition fields mean binding encoding and content schema, not key epochs. The future interface must also authenticate its selected envelope/key metadata and reject project/event/domain/content substitution. The proposed tuple alone supplies neither that metadata contract nor current project authority. Load the exact authorized same-project event before any reason projection; do not trust caller IDs to establish the relationship. [Proposal lines 27-31](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-authority-transaction-evidence/docs/agency-projects/privacy-lifecycle-representation-proposal.md:27) |
| Current Privacy case crypto reuse | **Reject for this Agency representation.** | Current Privacy AAD is `["warpdrive-privacy", VERSION, caseId, purpose]`, with only `intake`, `decision`, `identity`, `job`, `policy`. Its HMAC uses that case context and the current shared derived key. Passing project/event identifiers as a case or casting an Agency purpose would not implement the proposed contract. Ciphertext `VERSION = 1` is an envelope format, not a key epoch or key lookup reference. [Current pinned crypto](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/7e747e99524e08037da6eba1bd01f6558663f8f0/src/features/privacy/crypto.ts#L6-L38) |
| Envelope, key lookup and rotation | **Unselected / unsupported.** | No concrete Agency envelope/comparison interface, accepted format identifier, opaque-reference lookup, old-key availability rule, rekey writer, rotation/replay policy or key-destruction outcome exists in the inspected contract. No API name or key ID is supplied by this review. Retaining/removing a reference does not establish destruction of key material, per-entry cryptographic erasure or physical erasure. [Current decrypt path](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/7e747e99524e08037da6eba1bd01f6558663f8f0/src/features/privacy/crypto.ts#L41-L57), [prior owner decision](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-privacy-data-lifecycle/outputs/warpdrive-agency-core-contract-decision-6091c22.md) |
| Existing intent with missing comparison/result/key/tombstone material | **Accept mandatory non-reexecution as an invariant; recovery interface unselected.** | Current native project/parent authority must precede recovery disclosure. Once an existing logical intent is known, absent/unusable material must not convert it into a fresh command. The proposed bounded recovery-unavailable outcome is a reasonable design direction, but its exact public Result, lookup ordering, conflict behavior and observable timing remain unimplemented and unqualified. No new error code is selected. [Proposal line 35](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-authority-transaction-evidence/docs/agency-projects/privacy-lifecycle-representation-proposal.md:35) |
| Terminal record, expiry and restore | **Unselected; persistence remains blocked.** | If all evidence of an old intent is purged, the system needs a separately accepted way to prevent that intent becoming executable again. The proposal supplies no terminal record fields/lifetime, retained comparison policy, expiry behavior or backup/restore recovery protocol. No indefinite retention, automatic expiry or content resurrection is authorized. The existing pure lifecycle `restore` action returns an archived project to its recorded prior state; it grants no persisted restore, disposed-reason restoration, deleted-project recovery or backup acceptance. [Pinned pure destination](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/6855645499b5f5878f7b2d2eb431dd6e6d4b7fbc/src/features/agency-projects/projectLifecycle.ts#L59-L64), [proposal lines 35-41](/Users/ali/Documents/Codex/2026-10-31/warpdrive-agency-projects-implementation/outputs/agency-authority-transaction-evidence/docs/agency-projects/privacy-lifecycle-representation-proposal.md:35) |

The two exact candidate tuples reviewed above are:

```text
["agency-project-lifecycle-request",1,actorUserId,intentId,projectId,action,expectedRevision,reasonOrNull]
["agency-project-lifecycle-reason",1,projectId,historyEventId,"reason",1]
```

These are variable-bearing specification examples. They are not new callable interfaces, persisted formats, production key purposes or grants to import Privacy crypto.

## Findings and remaining evidence

No new internal contradiction was established between the proposal's eight actions/reason normalization and the pinned pure lifecycle/schema source. The proposal explicitly acknowledges that representation and enforcement are absent. The meaningful source-bound integration gaps are the raw reason in the pure policy receipt, the unresolved receipt `operation` namespace, separately enforceable fact/content mutation, authenticated envelope metadata and the durable non-reexecution policy after expiry/deletion/restore. None can be closed by selecting JSON arrays or column names alone.

Later source-bound qualification needs normalized equivalence after the actual ingress (UUID case, trimmed/omitted/accepted-empty reason), preserved accepted FA/DE/format characters and rejected invalid reasons, meaningful field-change conflicts under the selected intent namespace, domain/project/event/content/metadata substitution, unknown and rotated keys, required event/payload rollback, current-authority replay, disposed-result and late-retry refusal, terminal expiry and backup/restore replay. These are future acceptance cases, not prepared or executed tests from this review.

## Coverage, identifying references and acceptance boundary

`agency_projects`, `agency_project_members`, `agency_project_history` and `agency_project_requests` retain the prior proposed initial **`unsupported`, `candidate_links_only`** disposition. The optional `agency_project_history_content` receives that same proposed initial disposition only if separately selected and adopted. This review inserts no registry/catalog/coverage entry and no discovery reader map entry. Actual accepted combined source, exact table/writer/copy inventory, literal per-table coverage and qualified safe readers remain separate owner gates. [Current classification](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/7e747e99524e08037da6eba1bd01f6558663f8f0/src/features/privacy/registryClassification.ts#L14-L35), [capability rejection](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/7e747e99524e08037da6eba1bd01f6558663f8f0/src/features/privacy/registry.ts#L57-L71), [coverage scope](https://github.com/KhademOHAli1/warpdrive/blob/7e747e99524e08037da6eba1bd01f6558663f8f0/src/features/privacy/discoveryCoverage.ts#L3-L19).

Project, user, subject/contact/org/deal, event, recorder, intent, correlation, key-reference and disposition-provenance relationships remain identifying or correlating data. Project ownership is not sole subjecthood. No retained-field interval, principal replacement, cascade/SET NULL, blocked-dependency resolution or physical-delete success is selected. Archive/cancel, removed payload bytes, unavailable keys, hashes and minimal terminal records establish none of the physical/provider/backup erasure outcomes. Those evidence boundaries remain separate.

Only this local decision artifact was written. No Agency/repository code, packet, earlier review or ledger was edited; no tests, SQL, schema/DDL, builds, static checker, runtime, provider, allocation or enablement ran. No private key values or runtime personal data were read, and no reply was sent to another chat. Agency's full 12-package/96-task goal and Privacy's full DPL-01 through DPL-36 goal remain active with their existing acceptance gates.

Source byte identities additionally checked at the verified Agency commit: `projectLifecycle.ts` SHA-256 `e535c05920128b9e5b0bff1e4fe3dad566d42582f9a1c5c7afc22e4cc0f153d4`; `projectSchemas.ts` `3009adc5370e735f0e8f8214f7435f112859f1d73e4bebecbd9bb4a8b23922c5`; `valueSchemas.ts` `774f3f9b11de910292f530cda96b629a4cb9dec27b199632e11f445a076e9fef`. The current Privacy crypto bytes retain SHA-256 `7688c6e28320eb9a97b01a0ce7270c8959df59ad055b3b551148aa261886c4f4`; its identity helper retains `3e6e0d93648210dc8d6db22c0670d56e136a2c8bf005f445205ce8d506154a62`.
